00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:54.600
That will do

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.767
doesn’t it?

00:08:55.767 --> 00:08:57.200
This touches on an important concept

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.033
When we talked about syndrome differentiation

00:08:59.033 --> 00:09:01.400
we often used a kind of either-or thinking

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.767
just like binary opposition

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.167
It’s either yin or yang

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:05.133
black or white

00:09:05.133 --> 00:09:06.167
zero or one

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:07.533
This kind of mindset makes us wonder

00:09:07.533 --> 00:09:09.700
‘Am I experiencing excess in my heart or is it deficiency?’

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:10.533
But let me ask you

00:09:10.533 --> 00:09:11.867
If I give you a brief overview

00:09:11.867 --> 00:09:12.967
based on what we just talked about

00:09:12.967 --> 00:09:14.367
excess in the heart might include symptoms like

00:09:14.367 --> 00:09:16.300
heat, insomnia

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.733
and mouth sores

00:09:17.733 --> 00:09:20.633
while deficiency could involve waking up early

00:09:20.633 --> 00:09:21.900
and experiencing palpitations

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.167
Is it possible for a patient

00:09:23.167 --> 00:09:24.067
to experience both of these at the same time?

00:09:24.067 --> 00:09:24.967
Yeah, it’s pretty common for some people

00:09:24.967 --> 00:09:26.600
to have two symptoms at once

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.233
This happens a lot

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:29.467
so not everything is black and white

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:30.967
Symptoms have a certain balance

00:09:30.967 --> 00:09:32.600
and the same goes for

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.067
the scents used in medicine

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:35.900
I want to create a recipe

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.067
that the body likes

00:09:37.067 --> 00:09:39.200
but not just throwing in something like

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:39.933
ice cream, because you love sweets

00:09:39.933 --> 00:09:40.833
so I’ll just add in all the sweetness

00:09:40.833 --> 00:09:41.900
If you overdo it with sweetness, it’s just too much

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:42.933
and I’m not a fan of that either

00:09:42.933 --> 00:09:44.900
It seems like a Chinese medicine doctor

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.233
is kind of like interpreting what's going on

00:09:46.233 --> 00:09:47.933
with your symptoms

00:09:47.933 --> 00:09:48.900
Remember how we talked about

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.267
the left brain and right brain concept before

00:09:50.267 --> 00:09:51.800
The right brain is about what your body needs

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.367
while the left brain is what your mind wants

00:09:53.367 --> 00:09:55.100
It’s like the doctor is figuring out

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.500
what your body, or right brain

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.100
is craving

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.600
and then put together that specific flavor

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.167
It's not just about one particular flavor

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:03.133
being the ultimate solution

00:10:03.133 --> 00:10:03.733
Yes

00:10:03.733 --> 00:10:05.167
exactly

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:07.167
So the clinical approach

00:10:07.167 --> 00:10:09.400
used to starts with your symptoms like insomnia

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.000
and then determines which herbs can help with sleep

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:12.700
and calming effects

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.167
It shifts from choosing specific medications

00:10:14.167 --> 00:10:16.067
to assessing your current health condition and figuring out

00:10:16.067 --> 00:10:18.000
what kinds of flavors your body needs

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:18.867
Flavors

00:10:18.867 --> 00:10:21.033
To be precise, flavor combination

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:22.100
For example, with insomnia

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.633
it might be a combination of sour, salty, and bitter flavors

00:10:23.633 --> 00:10:25.733
The key is to combine these flavors in specific ways

00:10:25.733 --> 00:10:27.300
and use ingredients

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:28.933
that match these flavor profiles

00:10:28.933 --> 00:10:30.733
So you’ll see that

00:10:30.733 --> 00:10:32.633
when we first start cooking

00:10:32.633 --> 00:10:33.833
we usually follow recipes carefully

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:35.367
measuring out grams of this

00:10:35.367 --> 00:10:37.500
cutting how much of that

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.033
and figuring out just how much salt and sugar to add

00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:40.200
The recipes I dread the most are the ones that say 'a pinch of salt' or 'a dash of sugar.'

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.200
Huh?

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.567
What does that even mean?

00:10:42.567 --> 00:10:43.633
But actually

00:10:43.633 --> 00:10:45.367
as an experienced chefs

00:10:45.367 --> 00:10:45.833
they just taste as they go

00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:47.600
Taste it and they know ‘It’s not sour enough

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.400
, need to add a bit of sweetness in this.’

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.633
same as experienced Chinese medicine doctors

00:10:49.633 --> 00:10:50.567
while they take your pulse

00:10:50.567 --> 00:10:51.867
and might think the treatment needs a bit more of a certain flavor

00:10:51.867 --> 00:10:53.833
Our approach is based on solid evidence

00:10:53.833 --> 00:10:55.867
There's a book called ‘Tang Ye Jing Fa’

00:10:55.867 --> 00:10:57.100
What’s so special about this is that

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.367
the author of ‘Shang Han Lun,’ Zhang Zhongjing said that

00:10:59.367 --> 00:11:00.300
his formulas

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.000
were all based on it

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.100
Here's the twist, the author of the 'Tang Ye Jing Fa,'

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.367
Yi Yin

00:11:04.367 --> 00:11:06.400
wasn’t a doctor he was actually a chef

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.067
So, I believe that

00:11:07.067 --> 00:11:08.733
the fundamental principles of Chinese medicine

00:11:08.733 --> 00:11:10.633
are closely connected

00:11:10.633 --> 00:11:12.000
to these flavors

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.433
Take my trip to Spain as an example

00:11:14.433 --> 00:11:15.433
At that time

00:11:15.433 --> 00:11:17.467
I had just finished Dr. Xiao's workshop

00:11:17.467 --> 00:11:18.367
before heading there

00:11:18.367 --> 00:11:19.633
Well my trip was sort of

00:11:19.633 --> 00:11:21.200
a belly-belief journey

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.933
I was eating non-stop

00:11:23.933 --> 00:11:25.633
and ended up with a stomach flu

00:11:25.633 --> 00:11:26.733
At that time

00:11:26.733 --> 00:11:28.367
my stomach felt really bloated

00:11:28.367 --> 00:11:29.267
and uncomfortable

00:11:29.267 --> 00:11:31.033
and I didn’t have much Chinese medicine

00:11:31.033 --> 00:11:31.900
with me

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:32.533
So what did I do

00:11:32.533 --> 00:11:34.300
I decided to try olive oil

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.467
You know how in Europe

00:11:35.467 --> 00:11:38.300
there’s this trend of using olive oil for health

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.100
Well,

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:40.300
I had two types of olive oil with me

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.400
After trying them

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.167
I noticed that olive oil generally has a slightly sweet flavor

00:11:44.167 --> 00:11:46.367
But, extra virgin olive oil

00:11:46.367 --> 00:11:47.833
can also have a bit of a spicy kick

00:11:47.833 --> 00:11:49.767
due to the polyphenols in it

00:11:49.767 --> 00:11:50.867
I found that

00:11:50.867 --> 00:11:53.167
the olive oil with that sweet taste upfront

00:11:53.167 --> 00:11:54.867
and a spicy aftertaste

00:11:54.867 --> 00:11:57.267
actually worked better for relieving my bloating

00:11:57.267 --> 00:11:59.233
It made me think about what you said about the spleen

00:11:59.233 --> 00:12:01.300
and the flavor profile of the spleen-earth element—

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.200
the sweet, pungent and bitter of it

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.767
If I want to reduce the excess spleen energy

00:12:05.767 --> 00:12:07.767
like when there's too much food that's hard to digest

00:12:07.767 --> 00:12:09.833
I actually need to increase the pungent flavors in my diet

00:12:09.833 --> 00:12:12.167
A bit of kick from these flavors

00:12:12.167 --> 00:12:13.833
along with some strong

00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:14.600
spices

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.133
can really help my digestive system

00:12:17.133 --> 00:12:19.033
Sweeter type of olive oil

00:12:19.033 --> 00:12:20.500
can actually get a bit overwhelming when you eat it

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.433
That’s right

00:12:21.433 --> 00:12:22.800
So in this episode

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:24.767
we want to show you

00:12:24.767 --> 00:12:27.800
how to adjust flavors

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.667
based on your own situation

00:12:29.667 --> 00:12:30.533
For example

00:12:30.533 --> 00:12:32.867
if you try a herbal tea

00:12:32.867 --> 00:12:35.633
that seems to help you sleep better,

00:12:35.633 --> 00:12:37.133
but after drinking it

00:12:37.133 --> 00:12:38.667
you end up with a sore mouth

00:12:38.667 --> 00:12:39.267
and feel like

00:12:39.267 --> 00:12:41.333
you have excess heat, you might wonder if you should stop drinking it

00:12:41.333 --> 00:12:42.367
Well

00:12:42.367 --> 00:12:43.500
if you think about what we just discussed

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.967
the balance between excess and deficiency in relation to

00:12:44.967 --> 00:12:46.333
salty and bitter flavors

00:12:46.333 --> 00:12:47.833
most herbal teas if you look closely

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:48.800
focus on these three tastes

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.600
So Dr. Xiao

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.100
I’ve got a general idea now

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.633
about the scent ratios

00:12:52.633 --> 00:12:53.433
for insomnia

00:12:53.433 --> 00:12:55.200
I just found a herbal tea with calming effect

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:57.800
online at random

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.167
I should mention this is totally random

00:12:59.167 --> 00:12:59.567
believe it or not

00:12:59.567 --> 00:13:01.567
so if it happens to be spot on

00:13:01.567 --> 00:13:02.433
That’ll just be a coincidence

00:13:02.433 --> 00:13:03.833
This is the info ChatGPT provided

00:13:03.833 --> 00:13:05.233
We’re looking at a herbal tea

00:13:05.233 --> 00:13:07.267
related to calming and sleep

00:13:07.267 --> 00:13:08.933
Does it actually work?

00:13:08.933 --> 00:13:09.733
Let’s see what’s in the ingredient

00:13:09.733 --> 00:13:11.900
It contains chamomile

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:12.700
longan

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:13.600
rose

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.333
jasmine

00:13:14.333 --> 00:13:14.900
and monk fruit

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:15.600
Can you imagine

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.000
what this would taste like

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:17.900
We specifically chose something that

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.433
doesn't have a strong medicinal taste

00:13:19.433 --> 00:13:20.933
Longan, which we just talked about

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:22.167
is longan pulp

00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:23.933
has a sweet and slightly salty flavor

00:13:23.933 --> 00:13:24.733
As for other ingredients

00:13:24.733 --> 00:13:26.167
things like floral and fruity ingredients

00:13:26.167 --> 00:13:27.500
like monk fruit or flowers

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.367
they're generally more on the sour side

00:13:29.367 --> 00:13:30.267
So, it's really

00:13:30.267 --> 00:13:32.233
a combination of sour and salty flavors

00:13:32.233 --> 00:13:33.333
Based on this

00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.833
it definitely help soothe your mind

00:13:35.833 --> 00:13:36.933
That’s for sure

00:13:36.933 --> 00:13:38.633
The lesson here is

00:13:38.633 --> 00:13:39.700
just as we mentioned

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:41.433
like a chef tasting their dish

00:13:41.433 --> 00:13:43.733
one bite and you know how to adjust your flavors

00:13:43.733 --> 00:13:45.033
But how you can apply this

00:13:45.033 --> 00:13:45.867
on making herbal tea

00:13:45.867 --> 00:13:47.000
If you find that

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.567
drinking it helps you sleep a bit better

00:13:48.567 --> 00:13:49.333
but also makes your mouth sore

00:13:49.333 --> 00:13:50.000
What does it means

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.300
it might mean the tea is too strong

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:54.400
leaning toward excessive heat

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.733
In that case

00:13:55.733 --> 00:13:58.500
you should reduce the saltiness and increase the acidity

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.833
So, I'd really encourage you

00:13:59.833 --> 00:14:01.400
to cut back on the longan

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.067
or even leave it out entirely

00:14:03.067 --> 00:14:04.100
or just use a very small amount

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:05.867
You could also replace it with jujube

00:14:05.867 --> 00:14:06.867
or other sour herbs

00:14:06.867 --> 00:14:08.900
Right now, the only sour ingredients are monk fruit

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:09.700
and rose petals

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.700
You can even add something like

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.767
jujube seeds

00:14:11.767 --> 00:14:13.000
It might be better to achieve that

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.167
calming effect

00:14:14.167 --> 00:14:15.167
If you can't find jujube seeds

00:14:15.167 --> 00:14:17.400
you could use schisandra instead

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:18.067
Or even

00:14:18.067 --> 00:14:19.700
adding a bit of ume juice

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.300
which works well too

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:23.167
Basically, just add a bit more sourness

00:14:23.167 --> 00:14:24.600
So what if

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:27.667
I add a bit of balsamic vinegar

00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:29.233
Technically

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.200
theoretically it would work

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.767
but I really can’t picture

00:14:32.767 --> 00:14:34.567
adding balsamic vinegar to your herbal tea

00:14:34.567 --> 00:14:35.200
Like what?

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.200
What if

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.633
I add a bit of lemon

00:14:37.633 --> 00:14:38.233
Of course

00:14:38.233 --> 00:14:40.300
lemon zest or even citrus based

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:42.033
It can balance out

00:14:42.033 --> 00:14:43.600
the salty flavor

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:44.633
and increase the acidic taste

00:14:44.633 --> 00:14:46.800
This might make the tea less heating

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:47.400
and more soothing

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.200
By this you’ll not have excessive heat

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.067
which could potentially help you sleep better

00:14:51.067 --> 00:14:52.200
On the other hand

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.667
if you drink it

00:14:53.667 --> 00:14:55.633
and you do feel it’s easy to fall asleep

00:14:55.633 --> 00:14:57.433
but somehow feel cold

00:14:57.433 --> 00:14:58.233
and tired

00:14:58.233 --> 00:14:59.900
even feeling off during the day

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.167
or experiencing palpitations

00:15:02.167 --> 00:15:03.000
Here

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.400
I might think

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.367
Should I add something

00:15:05.367 --> 00:15:06.667
warmer to balance it out?

00:15:06.667 --> 00:15:07.800
But that’s a common misconception

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:08.633
A lot of people believe that

00:15:08.633 --> 00:15:10.200
if their body tends to be cold

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.600
then they shouldn’t drink certain things

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:13.267
Patients often say this to me

00:15:13.267 --> 00:15:14.200
but in reality

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:16.667
it might just be that the tea is too sour

00:15:16.667 --> 00:15:17.433
and not salty enough

00:15:17.433 --> 00:15:18.533
Remember we just mentioned

00:15:18.533 --> 00:15:19.767
salty flavors works like fuel

00:15:19.767 --> 00:15:21.233
that increase your internal heat

00:15:21.233 --> 00:15:22.767
make it burn brighter

00:15:22.767 --> 00:15:24.300
so you don't feel cold

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:24.833
So instead of

00:15:24.833 --> 00:15:26.933
adding spicy herbs

00:15:26.933 --> 00:15:29.167
you should lean more towards salty ones

00:15:29.167 --> 00:15:30.200
Like add a bit more longan

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.867
If you use longan along with jujube

00:15:31.867 --> 00:15:33.533
the overall effect of the herbs

00:15:33.533 --> 00:15:35.700
will shift towards warming

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.900
and excess heat

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.200
It can help improve

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.633
your mood, energy

00:15:40.633 --> 00:15:41.267
and sleep

00:15:41.267 --> 00:15:42.067
Some people might think of

00:15:42.067 --> 00:15:44.333
adding cinnamon

00:15:44.333 --> 00:15:44.833
etc.

00:15:44.833 --> 00:15:46.300
So what’ll happened if you use cinnamon

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.233
You need to know that

00:15:47.233 --> 00:15:49.233
cinnamon is actually a spicy ingredient

00:15:49.233 --> 00:15:50.900
not a salty one

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:52.400
When you added it

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:54.100
it might not be as effective

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.267
for calming the mind

00:15:55.267 --> 00:15:57.133
Spicy flavors don’t really affect

00:15:57.133 --> 00:15:58.867
the heart in terms of regulation

00:15:58.867 --> 00:16:00.567
so we usually opt for a bit more salty herbs

00:16:00.567 --> 00:16:01.333
just a bit more

00:16:01.333 --> 00:16:03.433
This is the misconception that we talked about earlier

00:16:03.433 --> 00:16:05.333
like I used to underestimate longan and jujube

00:16:05.333 --> 00:16:07.067
but in reality

00:16:07.067 --> 00:16:08.033
when used it wisely

00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:09.200
they can sometimes be

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:09.967
even more effective

00:16:09.967 --> 00:16:11.600
This shows that

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.167
if people rely only on

00:16:14.167 --> 00:16:15.067
cold, hot, warmth, and coolness

00:16:15.067 --> 00:16:16.167
they might think

00:16:16.167 --> 00:16:17.767
they’ve balanced things out

00:16:17.767 --> 00:16:19.133
but it might not actually achieve the intended therapeutic effect

00:16:19.133 --> 00:16:20.900
I think I get the overall idea here

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:23.600
I would like to ask

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:26.933
you mentioned that jujube and longan are both considered “salty”

00:16:26.933 --> 00:16:27.533
But the kind of "salty" you’re talking about

00:16:27.533 --> 00:16:29.167
in Chinese medicine

00:16:29.167 --> 00:16:30.833
seems a bit different

00:16:30.833 --> 00:16:31.933
from what most people think of as salty

00:16:31.933 --> 00:16:32.933
What does this means?

00:16:32.933 --> 00:16:34.333
I think the confusion

00:16:34.333 --> 00:16:35.500
comes from the fact that

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:37.700
in Chinese medicine

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.200
all foods and herbs

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.333
are categorized into five flavors: pungent, salty, sweet, sour, and bitter

00:16:42.333 --> 00:16:43.700
So, there’s always

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:45.167
some sort of leaning or nuance

00:16:45.167 --> 00:16:46.200
For instance

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.733
take salty flavor as example

00:16:47.733 --> 00:16:49.067
In cooking

00:16:49.067 --> 00:16:51.067
there's something called the Umami Flavor

00:16:51.067 --> 00:16:53.067
For example, foods that come from the ocean

00:16:53.067 --> 00:16:54.000
we’ll describe it as Umami

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.567
like clams

00:16:55.567 --> 00:16:56.767
or lobster

00:16:56.767 --> 00:16:57.667
are often said to have a Umami taste

00:16:57.667 --> 00:16:58.767
But do they really taste salty?

00:16:58.767 --> 00:16:59.933
In Chinese medicine

00:16:59.933 --> 00:17:02.000
we classify them as salty

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:02.800
Now

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:04.300
let's talk about sweet flavors

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:05.700
We mentioned earlier that longan

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.133
and jujube have a sweet flavor

00:17:07.133 --> 00:17:08.633
but there are other sweet flavors too

00:17:08.633 --> 00:17:10.100
like yam

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:10.933
and Job's tears

00:17:10.933 --> 00:17:11.967
Do these sweet flavors feel the same to you?

00:17:11.967 --> 00:17:13.333
Do you think they taste the same?

00:17:13.333 --> 00:17:13.967
It's sweet

00:17:13.967 --> 00:17:15.567
but one has a salty undertone

00:17:15.567 --> 00:17:16.933
while the other is purely sweet

00:17:16.933 --> 00:17:19.000
maybe even a little sour and more mild

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.567
Based on this concept

00:17:20.567 --> 00:17:21.567
you’ll see

00:17:21.567 --> 00:17:23.067
you can gradually understand about this saltiness

00:17:23.067 --> 00:17:24.367
by practice

00:17:24.367 --> 00:17:25.700
For example

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:26.633
if we compare longan and jujube

00:17:26.633 --> 00:17:27.667
and if I were to add a third one

00:17:27.667 --> 00:17:28.733
this is just my opinion

00:17:28.733 --> 00:17:30.067
maybe even a ripe mango could work

00:17:30.067 --> 00:17:31.267
If you have a mango at home that’s overripe

00:17:31.267 --> 00:17:33.100
you can add it to your herbal tea

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:33.700
Why

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:34.967
Because mangoes can increase

00:17:34.967 --> 00:17:36.300
the body's internal heat

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:37.733
We all know that when your skin isn't in great condition

00:17:37.733 --> 00:17:38.833
you shouldn't eat too much mango

00:17:38.833 --> 00:17:40.300
because it can cause flare-ups

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:41.900
But when you eat longan, it can cause mouth sores

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.133
because it actually has a bit of a salty taste

00:17:43.133 --> 00:17:44.267
Actually, it seems like

00:17:44.267 --> 00:17:46.500
when we talk about 'salty' in ancient times it wasn't just about the taste of salt

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.767
It included a richer, umami-like flavor

00:17:48.767 --> 00:17:50.133
something really intense

00:17:50.133 --> 00:17:51.433
and fresh

00:17:51.433 --> 00:17:53.467
This is what we called salty

00:17:53.467 --> 00:17:56.533
And back then, salty foods were believed to nourish the heart but also increase internal heat

00:17:56.533 --> 00:17:57.633
So, this is why

00:17:57.633 --> 00:17:59.600
you might be advised not to eat salty foods

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.067
when you have skin inflammation

00:18:01.067 --> 00:18:02.067
a cold

00:18:02.067 --> 00:18:04.067
or any condition that's causing excessive heat

00:18:04.067 --> 00:18:05.833
It's not about specific fruits

00:18:05.833 --> 00:18:07.800
or whether something is too cold

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:09.100
but rather about

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.100
the saltiness and its effects

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.700
We've put together a chart here

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.333
that covers the different types of flavors

00:18:15.333 --> 00:18:16.967
of some common ingredients we use

00:18:16.967 --> 00:18:18.600
It's a basic guide to help you get started with

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.967
understanding these flavors

00:18:20.967 --> 00:18:23.067
Think of it as a '1.0' version of how we use flavors to support the body

00:18:23.067 --> 00:18:25.033
We'll be diving deeper into this chart

00:18:25.033 --> 00:18:26.600
as we go along

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.767
Alright, so one last question for you, Dr. Xiao

00:18:28.767 --> 00:18:31.000
When it comes to sleep

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.867
how can I apply the concept

00:18:32.867 --> 00:18:33.633
What kind of dish

00:18:33.633 --> 00:18:36.500
could a mom cook using those flavors to help her kid or husband

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.733
who's been stressed about exams and not sleeping well

00:18:38.733 --> 00:18:40.333
Something that would invigorating heart

00:18:40.333 --> 00:18:41.933
and improve their sleep

00:18:41.933 --> 00:18:44.167
What we really want to bring to this episode is

00:18:44.167 --> 00:18:46.967
showing you how to practically apply this theory

00:18:46.967 --> 00:18:48.500
Not dreaming up

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:52.467
or making up a good herbal tea out of nothing

00:18:52.467 --> 00:18:53.533
Try it out yourself

00:18:53.533 --> 00:18:54.633
Think of something salty, sour, and bitter flavors

00:18:54.633 --> 00:18:56.200
In cooking

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.600
it’ll probably be

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.267
bitter might be something like bitter melon

00:18:59.267 --> 00:19:00.900
sour

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:01.733
could be pineapple

00:19:01.733 --> 00:19:02.800
and for salty

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.067
you might use pickled pineapple

00:19:04.067 --> 00:19:06.133
Pineapple with bitter melon soup—does that work?

00:19:06.133 --> 00:19:07.433
Yes, you’ll find that

00:19:07.433 --> 00:19:09.333
the recipe you randomly come up with

00:19:09.333 --> 00:19:10.067
like pineapple with bitter melon soup

00:19:10.067 --> 00:19:11.500
if you search online

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.733
you’ll definitely find it listed as something that clears heat and tranquilization

00:19:13.733 --> 00:19:14.467
Trust me

00:19:14.467 --> 00:19:16.200
and try it yourself

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.200
You can think of

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:18.867
any calming recipe in your mind

00:19:18.867 --> 00:19:19.900
and then look it up online

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:20.933
You'll definitely find

00:19:20.933 --> 00:19:23.400
it has calming effects and helps with heat-clearing and various other benefits

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.633
I often feel that

00:19:25.633 --> 00:19:28.133
these effects are actually a result of Chinese medicine theories

00:19:28.133 --> 00:19:30.033
It’s like how all ancient civilizations

00:19:30.033 --> 00:19:31.467
are often said to have developed along the

00:19:31.467 --> 00:19:32.867
Euphrates

00:19:32.867 --> 00:19:34.600
and Tigris rivers

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.467
Our civilization

00:19:35.467 --> 00:19:37.000
followed these two rivers as we developed

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.767
If traditional Chinese medicine were considered a civilization

00:19:38.767 --> 00:19:40.833
its origins would be in flavors

00:19:40.833 --> 00:19:43.400
The effectiveness of different ingredients

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.833
flows from these flavors

00:19:44.833 --> 00:19:46.733
So now

00:19:46.733 --> 00:19:48.033
we're giving you a glimpse into

00:19:48.033 --> 00:19:49.400
a more wider

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.333
more higher perspective

00:19:50.333 --> 00:19:51.867
With this

00:19:51.867 --> 00:19:54.333
you'll get a clearer view of how everything fits together

00:19:54.333 --> 00:19:55.067
Just now

00:19:55.067 --> 00:19:56.667
I had an interesting thought

00:19:56.667 --> 00:19:58.400
As you know, I really enjoy drinking coffee

00:19:58.400 --> 00:19:59.533
I’m planning to invite

00:19:59.533 --> 00:20:01.133
an amazing coffee roaster

00:20:01.133 --> 00:20:02.333
who was the first Asian

00:20:02.333 --> 00:20:04.733
to win the European Roasting Championship

00:20:04.733 --> 00:20:05.600
We'll talk more about that later

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.867
So, drinking coffee

00:20:06.867 --> 00:20:09.667
caffeine can cause insomnia, but

00:20:09.667 --> 00:20:10.967
some people

00:20:10.967 --> 00:20:12.567
including myself

00:20:12.567 --> 00:20:13.367
find that drinking high-quality coffee

00:20:13.367 --> 00:20:16.967
before bed actually helps them fall asleep easily

00:20:16.967 --> 00:20:19.033
I feel like it’s the same concept

00:20:19.033 --> 00:20:20.800
This is where we see

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:23.333
a different take between Western and traditional Chinese medicine

00:20:23.333 --> 00:20:24.300
or just a gap

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.467
in understanding the world

00:20:26.467 --> 00:20:28.467
if we only look at it from a material perspective

00:20:28.467 --> 00:20:30.300
I can’t say for sure

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:32.133
because there's no clinical research to back this up

00:20:32.133 --> 00:20:33.567
but from my observations

00:20:33.567 --> 00:20:35.400
a lot of patients have told me that

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.167
when they drink good coffee

00:20:37.167 --> 00:20:38.767
by that I mean coffee with certain characteristics flavor

00:20:38.767 --> 00:20:40.600
That is usually purer

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.600
and more complex

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.533
It’s not just overwhelmingly bitter

00:20:44.533 --> 00:20:46.533
instead, it might have floral

00:20:46.533 --> 00:20:47.400
or fruity notes

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:49.067
and the flavor changes from the start to the finish

00:20:49.067 --> 00:20:50.833
kind of like how perfume has different layers of scent

00:20:50.833 --> 00:20:53.367
People say that after drinking these coffees

00:20:53.367 --> 00:20:54.500
they actually feel relaxed

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:55.800
and even sleep better

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.067
From this perspective

00:20:57.067 --> 00:21:00.267
if a combination of sour, bitter, and salty flavors

00:21:00.267 --> 00:21:01.767
can help you sleep better

00:21:01.767 --> 00:21:03.533
why can't coffee, which has these flavors

00:21:03.533 --> 00:21:04.333
do the same?

00:21:04.333 --> 00:21:06.333
From the standpoint of caffeine

00:21:06.333 --> 00:21:07.367
coffee

00:21:07.367 --> 00:21:09.200
is usually considered bad for sleep

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.200
However, if you look at it from a flavor perspective

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.500
this combination of tastes

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:15.033
might have the desired effect

00:21:15.033 --> 00:21:16.633
Maybe we can try to

00:21:16.633 --> 00:21:17.600
explain it this way

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:18.867
So let me break it down

00:21:18.867 --> 00:21:20.633
When we talk about flavors like sour, bitter, and salty

00:21:20.633 --> 00:21:22.067
salty as we mentioned

00:21:22.067 --> 00:21:24.167
tends to have a rich, sweet aftertaste

00:21:24.167 --> 00:21:25.600
I believe that a good coffee should have that

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:27.333
fresh, sweet aftertaste

00:21:27.333 --> 00:21:28.467
along with a hint of bitterness

00:21:28.467 --> 00:21:29.567
I’ve noticed that

00:21:29.567 --> 00:21:31.900
the difference between good coffee and regular coffee is that

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:33.267
In terms of an antioxidant perspective

00:21:33.267 --> 00:21:35.267
good coffee has enough polyphenols

00:21:35.267 --> 00:21:36.767
and Chlorogenic acid

00:21:36.767 --> 00:21:38.867
which are antioxidants that can actually help with sleep

00:21:38.867 --> 00:21:41.167
This is how I used to understand it from a chemical perspective

00:21:41.167 --> 00:21:42.133
But now we know that

00:21:42.133 --> 00:21:43.800
Chlorogenic acid gives a sour taste

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.800
and polyphenols add a bit of bitterness

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.933
and good coffee has that salty touch

00:21:47.933 --> 00:21:49.233
which together

00:21:49.233 --> 00:21:51.000
create a perfect blend for soothing insomnia

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:51.567
Exactly

00:21:51.567 --> 00:21:53.800
So, imagine if ancient people were tasting coffee

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:55.633
though they probably didn’t

00:21:55.633 --> 00:21:57.333
but just imagine

00:21:57.333 --> 00:21:58.600
They might not have been able to identify things like

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.333
Chlorogenic acid

00:22:00.333 --> 00:22:03.233
but they might have noticed

00:22:03.233 --> 00:22:04.267
the coffee's sour taste

00:22:04.267 --> 00:22:05.867
and might have thought that this could be used to help with insomnia

00:22:05.867 --> 00:22:07.367
So, if you find that coffee

00:22:07.367 --> 00:22:08.500
doesn’t have that salty

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:10.500
and sweet aftertaste

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:12.667
it’s best to avoid drinking it after 3 PM

00:22:12.667 --> 00:22:14.633
The caffeine in it

00:22:14.633 --> 00:22:16.333
is likely to be a major cause

00:22:16.333 --> 00:22:17.367
of insomnia

00:22:17.367 --> 00:22:17.933
But it depends

00:22:17.933 --> 00:22:20.000
if you're drinking coffee to stay awake, then that's one thing

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:23.133
But after hearing all this

00:22:23.133 --> 00:22:24.333
it really feels like

00:22:24.333 --> 00:22:27.200
Chinese medicine makes things seem very complex

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:29.600
Yes it has a lot of depth and knowledge

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:32.000
but there's this idea

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:33.333
that simplicity is key

00:22:33.333 --> 00:22:34.300
it all boils down to something simple—

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:36.933
Chinese medicine in every bite

00:22:36.933 --> 00:22:39.733
So, let's use this concept

00:22:39.733 --> 00:22:41.533
and insomnia as a way

00:22:41.533 --> 00:22:44.267
to give everyone a glimpse into the fundamental principles of Chinese medicine

00:22:44.267 --> 00:22:45.900
how the five flavors can help balance the body

